346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Messaging In our task analysis and application prototype, we have included a feature where potential tenants and renters are able to message one another to discuss the details of listings and set up walk-throughs. One option for implementing this feature is to base the UI off Bootstrap like this example on JSFiddle. Then, when a user writes a message to another user, we store the message in our database. We also poll the database to look for any new messages; when we find then, we insert them into a container in the view as HTML elements using jQuery. We would use the overflow property in Bootstrap to get the messages to vertically scroll. If this is difficult to maintain in real-time, we may also want to open a websocket, so the user is able to listen for and send messages and persist messages in our database layer. )
/E (Messaging In our task analysis and application prototype, we have included a feature where potential tenants and renters are able to message one another to discuss the details of listings and set up walk-throughs. One option for implementing this feature is to base the UI off Bootstrap like this example on JSFiddle. Then, when a user writes a message to another user, we store the message in our database. We also poll the database to look for any new messages; when we find then, we insert them into a container in the view as HTML elements using jQuery. We would use the overflow property in Bootstrap to get the messages to vertically scroll. If this is difficult to maintain in real-time, we may also want to open a websocket, so the user is able to listen for and send messages and persist messages in our database layer. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
